WEBVTT

00:01:58.906 --> 00:02:00.366
You don’t need a whole agenda;

00:02:00.366 --> 00:02:01.951
nobody’s going to read it anyway.

00:02:01.951 --> 00:02:05.246
But that purpose statement
is enough  so that when you start,

00:02:05.246 --> 00:02:08.749
everybody is sitting up, paying attention
and focused on the goal.

00:02:09.041 --> 00:02:10.334
Tip number two:

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:12.920
invite the least number
of people possible.

00:02:13.379 --> 00:02:14.380
Let’s be honest,

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:16.841
most of us invite people
to meetings defensively.

00:02:17.049 --> 00:02:18.759
We know that Raco’s the one we need

00:02:18.759 --> 00:02:20.845
but if Dion doesn’t feel
like he’s involved,

00:02:20.845 --> 00:02:22.013
he’s going to be cranky,

00:02:22.013 --> 00:02:24.307
so you invite him
and then Shannon and then Jane.

00:02:24.307 --> 00:02:26.559
And now we’re wasting
all of these people’s time

00:02:26.559 --> 00:02:29.061
instead of just going
directly to the decision maker.

00:02:29.061 --> 00:02:31.689
It’s time to let go 
of those grade-school fears